From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:39:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Use the content blocker patches: trusted lists,
 resources, and Block Element

Patches/ladybird 0004-0009 let Ladybird's content blocker apply uBlock
Origin's scriptlets, procedural filters, $redirect surrogates,
$removeparam, $popup and CNAME filters. This puts them to use.

Meta/update-filter-lists.py now converts the lists for the patched
engine, so they keep the filters the stock engine had to drop. uBlock
Origin's own lists go in trusted-lists/, which UI/FilterLists.cpp passes
as --trusted-content-blocker-list so they may use the scriptlets uBO
reserves for its lists, and uBO's scriptlets and redirect surrogates go
in resources/, passed as --content-blocker-resources. Meta/check.py knows
the new layout.

The context menu's new Block Element... action ends in a dialog that
shows the picked element's filter for the user to edit and add to the
custom filters (UI/ElementPicker.cpp).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
